# =====================================================================
#  Alkemos — Environment variables
#  Copy this file to `.env.local` for local dev, or set the same keys
#  in your Vercel project settings → Environment Variables.
# =====================================================================

# --- Supabase (required for production auth + data) ---
# Find these in your Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR-ANON-PUBLIC-KEY
# (The ops scripts scripts/db-backup.mjs · db-restore.mjs · retro-pair-blog.mjs
# also accept SUPABASE_URL as an alias of NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL.)

# When the two keys above are missing, the app runs in a local-only
# "demo mode" backed by localStorage — useful for previews & testing.
# Two demo accounts are auto-seeded in demo mode (source: src/lib/data/auth.ts):
#   ahmed@coach.app / coach123   (logs in as the coach)
#   client@demo.app / client123  (logs in as a demo client)

# --- Email sending (Brevo REST API — HTTPS; Vercel serverless blocks
#     outbound SMTP ports 25/465/587, so the REST API over 443 is used) ---
# Used by POST /api/send-email to deliver tool results to visitors.
# Already configured on Vercel (owner) — same free Brevo account that
# serves the Supabase custom SMTP relay (auth emails). Free tier: 300/day.
BREVO_API_KEY=xkeysib-your-brevo-api-key
EMAIL_FROM="Alkemos <no-reply@alkemos.com>"
# Optional reply-to override (SET in Vercel production):
EMAIL_REPLY_TO=support@alkemos.com


# =====================================================================
# =====================================================================
#  AI System (OpenRouter + Groq + NVIDIA NIM + Gemini + Cloudflare
#  Workers AI — FIVE generation providers through one unified layer; +
#  Tavily and Exa as the SEARCH arms. GEMINI-FIRST LAW (343) CANCELLED
#  2026-10-31 by owner order «إلغاء قانون Gemini-First نهائيًا، بما يشمل
#  السلاسل الثقيلة» (Phase 5-A): gemini rides both chains as an ordinary
#  TAIL entry (never a lead — the 3-way rotation openrouter → groq →
#  nvidia leads). TAVILY joined 2026-10-31 (Phase 5-A) and EXA joined
#  2026-10-31 (Phase 5-B) — the §6-أ language-split grounded-search
#  ladder landed its FINAL state: EN exa → tavily → groq → gemini dormant
#  · AR tavily → groq → exa (English-equivalent query) → gemini dormant.
#  CLOUDFLARE WORKERS AI joined 2026-10-31 (Phase 5-C / stage ج — owner
#  order «نفّذ جميع المراحل المتبقية» approving §12-3): the FIFTH
#  provider, FIRST-WAVE AGILE ROLES ONLY (blog:pairing → 70b-fp8-fast ·
#  blog:latin-tokens-ar → scout; never the heavy chains, never the
#  streaming/fast chain — no streaming in JSON mode). NO provider holds
#  a forced priority — every slot is a measured task-type/efficiency/
#  availability decision and every arm fails over honestly.)
# =====================================================================
#
# The platform talks to EXACTLY FIVE generation providers through a single
# unified layer (src/lib/ai-provider.ts) + TWO search providers (Tavily,
# Exa — search/extraction ONLY, never generators):
#
#   1. OpenRouter  -> free models chain, rotation lead #1 (OPENROUTER_API)
#   2. Groq        -> interleaved fallback, rotation lead #2 (GROQ_API_KEY)
#   3. NVIDIA NIM  -> integrate.api.nvidia.com, rotation lead #3
#                     (NVIDIA_API_KEY)
#   4. GEMINI      -> native REST (x-goog-api-key), NOT OpenAI-shape —
#                     TAIL entry of both chains + DORMANT last arm of the
#                     grounded-search walk (GEMINI_API_KEY)
#   +. TAVILY      -> search/extraction ONLY (never a generator) — the
#                     FIRST arm of the §6-أ AR ladder and #2 on EN
#                     (TAVILY_API_KEY; free Researcher plan, basic search
#                     = 1 credit of 1000/month, NO card)
#   +. EXA         -> search/extraction ONLY (never a generator) — the
#                     FIRST arm of the §6-أ EN ladder and #3 on AR with
#                     the English-equivalent query (EXA_API_KEY; free
#                     $10/month recurring credit, NO card) + the optional
#                     /contents full-text deepening
#   5. CLOUDFLARE  -> Workers AI REST (/accounts/{id}/ai/run/{model}),
#                     NOT OpenAI-shape — FIRST-WAVE AGILE ROLES ONLY:
#                     the blog:pairing chain tag leads with
#                     llama-3.3-70b-instruct-fp8-fast and the
#                     blog:latin-tokens-ar tag leads with
#                     llama-4-scout-17b-16e-instruct (the Phase-3
#                     measured picks; llama-3.1-8b* EXCLUDED from every
#                     JSON role — its json_object failed parsing and its
#                     json_schema was refused by the API). Free tier
#                     10,000 neurons/day, NO card. The shared neuron
#                     meter (src/lib/ai-cf-usage.ts) counts every call:
#                     WARNING at ≥80% (queue-health strip) · BARRIER at
#                     ≥95% skips every new CF call honestly and the role
#                     falls to the ordinary chain.
#
# Missing GEMINI_API_KEY = the chain skips the gemini entries without
# consuming attempt budget. Missing TAVILY_API_KEY / EXA_API_KEY = that
# search arm fails honestly and the grounded walk falls through to the
# next arm (rollback without code). The OpenAI / Anthropic / DeepSeek direct integrations
# remain REMOVED. If you want a Google model via OpenRouter, the
# google/gemma-* ids stay DEAD (Phase 177 purge) — use the native gemini
# arm instead.
#
# Gemini usage is tracked per-tag to Upstash (UPSTASH pair below) and
# reported weekly in docs/ai/gemini-weekly-usage-report.md.
#
# NOTE the exact spelling: the OpenRouter key env var is
#   OPENROUTER_API        <- used by the code (and older docs)
#   OPENROUTER_API_KEY    <- accepted as an alias of the above
# Set at least ONE of them, plus GROQ_API_KEY and NVIDIA_API_KEY for
# full reliability (the same keys live in Vercel Production and GitHub
# Actions secrets).
#
# Optional overrides:
# AI_PROVIDER=openrouter      # openrouter | groq | nvidia | gemini
# AI_MODEL=                   # force a specific model for getEnvConfig()
# AI_BASE_URL=                # custom OpenAI-compatible endpoint

OPENROUTER_API=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=        # alias of OPENROUTER_API (either works)
GROQ_API_KEY=
NVIDIA_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=             # optional tail provider (no forced priority — owner order 2026-10-31);
                            # GEMINI_API_KEY2 RETIRED permanently by the same owner order — no second
                            # Gemini key is needed and no code path may read one.
GEMINI_MODEL=               # optional (default gemini-3.5-flash since Phase 344; was gemini-3.8-flash)
GEMINI_GROUNDED_MODELS=     # optional (blog recovery 2026-10-16): comma-separated alternate models for the
                            # grounded-search ladder AFTER the default (built-in cross-family tail: gemini-3.8-flash,
                            # gemini-3.5-flash-lite — each family bills its OWN quota bucket, so a 429 on one
                            # falls through to the next REAL googleSearch-grounded call; live-probed retirements:
                            # gemini-2.5-flash 404 «no longer available to new users» · gemini-3.8-pro 404 «not
                            # found for API version v1beta» on the live key — both excluded since measured).
                            # Source: src/lib/ai-provider.ts, callGeminiGroundedSearch.
GEMINI_GROUNDED_ENABLED=    # optional (PHASE 5-A 2026-10-31, §6-أ): "0" REMOVES the dormant gemini googleSearch
                            # arm from the grounded-search walk without a deploy (it is the DORMANT LAST arm since
                            # the ladder re-order — 0/114 measured grounded successes on the free tier; the cooldown
                            # registry makes re-trying it cheap). Empty/absent = the arm stays in the walk as the
                            # last resort. Source: src/lib/ai-provider.ts, groundedArmOrder.

# --- Tavily search arm (PHASE 5-A 2026-10-31 — the FIRST arm of the §6-أ
#     grounded-search ladder: tavily → groq browser_search → gemini dormant;
#     the openrouter web arm was REMOVED from the effective ladder — dead
#     default model 404 + paid plugin 402). Tavily is a SEARCH/EXTRACTION
#     provider, never a generator: callTavilySearch runs a REAL basic search
#     (1 credit of the Researcher plan's free 1000/month — NO card, NO paid
#     service) whose live result URLs ARE the evidence, then synthesizes the
#     research JSON on the ordinary generation chain grounded on those REAL
#     results. Absent key = the arm fails honestly and the walk falls to
#     groq (rollback without code; §10-أ). ---
TAVILY_API_KEY=             # required for the search arm (repo Actions secret since Phase 3; the blog
                            # workflows + the grounded-failover probe pass it)
TAVILY_SEARCH_DEPTH=        # optional: "basic" (default — 1 credit, the measured Phase-3 shape) or
                            # "advanced" (2 credits — owner opt-in, no deploy).
TAVILY_MAX_RESULTS=         # optional: results per search (default 10; 1..20).
TAVILY_INCLUDE_DOMAINS=     # optional: comma-separated domain restriction (Phase-3 measured include_domains
                            # honored 100% with the 14 authority domains). EMPTY by default — the discovery
                            # research query stays unrestricted; the authority-domain law lives at the P4/P5
                            # citation gates where it belongs.

# --- Exa search arm (PHASE 5-B 2026-10-31 — the FIRST arm of the §6-أ EN
#     grounded-search ladder: exa → tavily → groq browser_search → gemini
#     dormant; on the AR ladder it is the THIRD arm and searches with the
#     ENGLISH-equivalent query — Exa's semantic map measured 2/40 Arabic
#     results, so Arabic intents map onto the English science literature).
#     Exa is a SEARCH/EXTRACTION provider, never a generator:
#     callExaSearch runs a REAL semantic search (POST api.exa.ai/search
#     {query, numResults, type:"auto"} — the Phase-3 measured shape:
#     80/80 results, 46% authority domains, μ=529ms) whose live result
#     URLs ARE the evidence (law 344), then the §6-أ OPTIONAL full-text
#     deepening (Exa /contents {ids: top-3, text:{maxCharacters}} with
#     Tavily /extract as the documented alternative extractor — a failed
#     deepening = a snippets-only bundle stamped researchDepth:"snippets",
#     NEVER an article failure), then the research-JSON synthesis on the
#     ordinary generation chain grounded on those REAL results. FREE plan:
#     $10/month recurring usage credit, NO card, NO paid service (expected
#     blog load ~$2–5/month). Absent key = the arm fails honestly and the
#     walk falls to tavily/groq (rollback without code; §10-ب). ---
EXA_API_KEY=                # required for the search arm (repo Actions secret since Phase 3; the blog
                            # workflows + the grounded-failover probe pass it)
EXA_NUM_RESULTS=            # optional: results per search (default 10 — the Phase-3 battery shape).
EXA_CONTENTS_MAX_CHARS=     # optional: per-page full-text cap for the /contents deepening AND the Tavily
                            # raw_content full-text clamp (default 5000; 500..20000 — the §6-أ "~5000" design).
EXA_INCLUDE_DOMAINS=        # optional: comma-separated domain restriction (Exa supports includeDomains
                            # officially; honored share measured live by the grounded-failover probe §13-6).
                            # EMPTY by default — the discovery query stays unrestricted; the authority-domain
                            # law lives at the P4/P5 citation gates where it belongs.
GROUNDED_ARM_ORDER=         # optional (PHASE 5-B diagnostics/rollback): overrides the whole grounded-search
                            # walk order without a deploy — a comma subset of exa,tavily,groq,gemini (e.g.
                            # "tavily,groq" to bypass the exa arm). Empty/invalid = the built-in §6-أ
                            # language-split ladder. Source: src/lib/ai-provider.ts, groundedArmOrder.

P0_PAIR_GAP_MS=             # optional (blog recovery 2026-10-20 — P0-PAIR-SERIAL): recovery gap in ms between
                            # the TWO languages' grounded research walks in the P0 CREATE path. The pair now runs
                            # SEQUENTIALLY (never Promise.all-concurrent — two simultaneous agentic walks on the
                            # single working free-tier grounded arm starved each other and killed 15 daily runs);
                            # when the first language lands on groq, the twin waits this gap for the per-minute
                            # token/tool bucket to recover. Default 90000 (measured-safe); 0 disables the gap
                            # (serialization itself is unconditional); ceiling clamps at 600000.
                            # Source: src/lib/blog-research.ts, runBilingualResearchPair.

# --- Cross-provider grounded-search failover (BLOG-PROVIDER-FAILOVER
#     2026-10-16; ladder RE-ORDERED PHASE 5-A 2026-10-31, owner order
#     «تنفيذ ذراع البحث Tavily»; FINAL language-split state PHASE 5-B
#     2026-10-31, owner order «دمج وتفعيل Exa») — P0 research walks
#     REAL-search arms in the §6-أ order, split by language:
#     EN: exa(search API, own free credit + chain synthesis) →
#         tavily(search API) → groq(browser_search) → gemini(DORMANT);
#     AR: tavily(search API) → groq(browser_search — GROQ-2 2026-10-17:
#         the compound-successor tool) → exa(search API WITH THE
#         English-equivalent query) → gemini(googleSearch, DORMANT last
#         arm). The openrouter web-plugin arm was REMOVED from the
#         effective ladder (dead default model 404 + paid plugin 402 —
#         P0-2); NVIDIA NIM is honestly excluded (no web-search tool in
#         its chat API). Every slot is a MEASURED task-type/efficiency/
#         availability decision — NO forced provider priority (owner order
#         2026-10-31). Every arm enforces the live-evidence gate — no
#         plain generation or fake results can pass as research. Keys: the
#         EXISTING provider keys + TAVILY_API_KEY + EXA_API_KEY per arm. ---
OPENROUTER_GROUNDED_MODEL=  # optional: model for the OpenRouter web-plugin grounded arm
                            # (default nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b:free — an existing
                            # live-verified free-chain id). The web plugin bills per-search
                            # credits on the existing key; no credits → honest 402 → groq arm.
GROQ_GROUNDED_MODEL=        # optional (GROQ-2 2026-10-17): LEADER model for the Groq grounded
                            # arm (default openai/gpt-oss-120b — the browser_search built-in
                            # tool; Groq DECOMMISSIONED the compound system 2026-09-21, so the
                            # old default compound-beta 404s permanently).
GROQ_GROUNDED_MODELS=       # optional (GROQ-2 2026-10-17): comma-separated FALLBACK models for
                            # the Groq grounded ladder AFTER the leader (built-in tail:
                            # openai/gpt-oss-20b). Each entry is a REAL browser_search call —
                            # a dead/drained id falls through to the next live model.
AI_PROVIDER_COOLDOWN_MS=    # optional (blog workflows set 1800000): quota-cooldown window for the
                            # provider failover — exhaustion-class failures (429/402/401/403/404)
                            # cool the failed provider/key×model and the chain/grounded walk SKIPS
                            # it (no futile repeat, no attempt-budget burn). ABSENT = disabled =
                            # byte-identical pre-2026-10-16 behavior. Kill-switch: AI_PROVIDER_COOLDOWN=0.
AI_PROVIDER_COOLDOWN=       # optional: set to 0 to force-disable the cooldown registry (rollback).
AI_METER=                   # optional (AI-Router unification R2, owner order 2026-10-31): "0" disables
                            # the centralized (provider×model×function) attempt meter COMPLETELY — no
                            # [ai-meter] console lines, no ai:usage:{date}:* Upstash keys, and no
                            # Tavily/Exa monthly quota counters. Fail-open by construction: a metering
                            # outage NEVER delays or disables generation. Source: src/lib/ai-usage-meter.ts.
AI_ROUTER_MODE=             # optional (AI-Router unification R3→R5): "legacy" serves the FROZEN
                            # pre-migration option blocks instead of the ai-registry policies (the
                            # rollback path without a deploy). Absent = "registry" (central source).

# --- Cloudflare Workers AI — FIFTH provider (Phase 5-C / stage ج,
#     owner order 2026-10-31 «نفّذ جميع المراحل المتبقية» approving §12-3) ---
# FIRST-WAVE AGILE ROLES ONLY (never the heavy generation chains, never
# the streaming/fast chain): blog:pairing leads with
# @cf/meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct-fp8-fast · blog:latin-tokens-ar leads
# with @cf/meta/llama-4-scout-17b-16e-instruct. Free tier 10,000
# neurons/day, NO card. Repo Actions secrets since the Phase-3 live
# battery (the two legacy zone-scoped cfut_ tokens carry NO Workers-AI
# permission and are NOT used). Neuron meter: cf:usage:{date}:neurons in
# Upstash (same store as the Gemini counters) — WARNING ≥80% (queue-health)
# · BARRIER ≥95% skips every new CF call honestly. Missing secrets or
# CF_ARM_ENABLED=0 → the role entries are skipped without consuming
# attempt budget and the ordinary chain serves the call (rollback without
# code).
CLOUDFLARE_AI_TOKEN=        # required for the CF role arm (repo Actions secret since Phase 3;
                            # Bearer auth on api.cloudflare.com/client/v4)
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=      # required for the CF role arm (the /accounts/{id}/ai/run/ path)
CF_ARM_ENABLED=             # optional: 0 = kill switch — fully disables the CF role arm without
                            # a deploy (zero-effect rollback; default on)
AI_COOLDOWN_STATE_FILE=     # optional: path of the cooldown state file (default
                            # ${TMPDIR}/alkemos-ai-provider-cooldown.json) — persists across the
                            # steps of one GitHub Actions job; contains NO secrets.

# --- Supabase service role (SERVER-ONLY — cron routes + admin APIs) ---
# Grants FULL DB access bypassing RLS. NEVER prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_,
# never expose to the browser, never commit a real value. Required by
# the blog pipeline cron routes (/api/cron/blog/*), the AI-jobs runner
# and the admin server routes. Find it in Supabase → Project Settings
# → API → service_role key. Also a GitHub Actions secret
# (SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY) for the native runners.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Site URL (public metadata base) ---
# Used by sitemap, OG images, RSS, email links, canonical tags.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://alkemos.com

# --- Cloudflare edge purge (BLOG-CACHE-REFRESH 2026-10-21) ---
# Powers the fail-soft targeted purge (by-URL, NOT a cache-settings
# change) in src/lib/blog-cache-revalidate.ts: after the owner approves
# a review or saves an edit, the article/listing/RSS/sitemap URLs are
# purged from the Cloudflare edge so readers see the change immediately
# instead of after the s-maxage=3600 window. Production values live in
# /srv/alkemos/shared/.env (appended via the dispatch-only
# ops-server-env-append.yml workflow with a names-only verify). When
# either var is absent the purge is skipped HONESTLY (reported in the
# API echo; the edge then self-heals within s-maxage).
# Zone: alkemos.com (b4be55a0736831d9c5d9564788861076) — token: a
# zone-scoped Cache Purge API token (cfut_… format).
CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID=
CLOUDFLARE_PURGE_TOKEN=

# --- Cron auth + scheduler independence (SCHEDULE HEALTH LAW §8) ---
# CRON_SECRET: shared secret for /api/cron/* routes (Vercel Cron sends
# it as Authorization: Bearer). Also a GitHub Actions secret.
# GITHUB_DISPATCH_TOKEN: fine-grained GitHub PAT (THIS repo only,
# Actions: Read and write ONLY) letting /api/cron/dispatch-pipelines
# top up missed blog pipeline slots and rescue the ai-jobs worker when
# GitHub's scheduler de-registers. Vercel env only — never a repo secret.
CRON_SECRET=
GITHUB_DISPATCH_TOKEN=

# --- Blog images (IMAGE SOURCE LAW v3 — Pexels-first) ---
# AI image generation is RETIRED (law v3); every blog image is real
# stock photography. PEXELS_API_KEY is the PRIMARY source (required in
# GitHub Actions secrets AND Vercel Production); Unsplash/Pixabay are
# failover. Pixabay queries run with safesearch=true (modesty law).
PEXELS_API_KEY=
UNSPLASH_ACCESS_KEY=
PIXABAY_API_KEY=

# --- EVO coach follow-up email (Phase 166/170 — opt-in, live) ---
# Master switch for /api/evo/followup/dispatch (404 when not "true").
# EVO_FOLLOWUP_FROM overrides the sender (default evo@alkemos.com,
# send-only); EVO_CRON_SECRET is that route's own x-cron-secret — a
# SEPARATE, independently-rotatable secret from CRON_SECRET, verified
# with the same timing-safe comparison (P1-6; SECURITY.md §3.3).
EVO_FOLLOWUP_ENABLED=
# Both set in Vercel production (FROM is the send-only sender,
# EVO_CRON_SECRET is independently rotatable from CRON_SECRET):
EVO_FOLLOWUP_FROM=evo@alkemos.com
EVO_CRON_SECRET=

# --- Blog research note (PHASE 5-A 2026-10-31) ---
# Blog P0 research rides the cross-provider grounded-search walk (Tavily
# search API first, then groq browser_search, gemini dormant last) — see
# the TAVILY block above for the arm's env vars.

# --- Blog AR Latin-repair rollback (R2, 2026-09-29 — NOT a secret) ---
# EMPTY/absent (default) = the localized repair: deterministic
# dictionary pass first, then a token-only small conversion call
# (Groq-eligible). Set to "1" ONLY to roll back to the pre-R2
# full-article repair call (debug/rollback lever; the gates are
# byte-identical either way). Documented in SECURITY.md §2.2.
LATIN_REPAIR_LEGACY=

# --- R3 Groq per-entry clamp rollback (Execution-Path Audit 2026-09-29) ---
# EMPTY/absent (default) = the R3 per-entry clamp: when a call's estimated
# size exceeds Groq's 8k TPM window, groq entries STAY in the chain with
# their own max_tokens clamped to the remaining window — kept only while
# the clamp stays >= 3800 output tokens (P2 content re-enters Groq; P4
# review stays openrouter/nvidia-only by design). Set to "0" ONLY to roll
# back to the pre-R3 behavior (drop ALL groq entries when the estimate
# exceeds the window). Documented in SECURITY.md §2.2 + AGENTS.md §8.
GROQ_MAX_TOKENS_CLAMP=

# --- PayPal (Primary Payment Method) ---
# Sandbox mode is used for development. Live mode will be enabled later.
#
# SECURITY:
# - PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET is SERVER-ONLY. Never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# - PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID is also server-only (used for server-side Order API).
# - NEXT_PUBLIC_PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID is the PUBLIC client ID used by the
#   PayPal JS SDK in the browser (safe to expose — PayPal's design).
#
# Obtain these from: https://developer.paypal.com/dashboard/applications/sandbox
# Create a Sandbox app → get Client ID + Secret + Webhook ID.
#
# Set these in Vercel → Project Settings → Environment Variables.
# Do NOT commit real Sandbox or Live credentials to Git.

PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=
PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET=
PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID=
PAYPAL_MODE=sandbox
NEXT_PUBLIC_PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=

# ============================================================
# Optional: public analytics + ads + coach promotion allowlist
# (P3-2, deep-audit confirmed 24 — Phase 217: these were documented in
# README's setup table but missing here, so local clones warned about
# every one of them).
# ============================================================
# Google Analytics 4 measurement ID (public by design — NEXT_PUBLIC_).
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=
# Google AdSense publisher id (ca-pub-…, public by design).
NEXT_PUBLIC_ADSENSE_CLIENT=
# Comma-separated allowlist: emails here are auto-promoted to coach on
# signup (coach_emails table, 0017 — never downgrades an admin).
COACH_EMAILS=

# ============================================================
# Optional: distributed rate limiting (Upstash Redis free tier)
# Shared rate-limit counters across serverless instances via REST.
# Falls back to per-instance in-memory Map when unset.
# Console: https://console.upstash.com -> Create Database -> REST API
# ============================================================
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
